## Standards

**P2 — Preserve quarantine during the newly enabled unsigned whole-app update.** Changed contract `docs/PRODUCT_CONTRACTS.md:76` explicitly requires “Preserve quarantine and require the user's per-app macOS allow action”; changed guidance `docs/distribution/DESKTOP.md:79` also promises that the updater preserves quarantine. The newly accepted unsigned path in `apps/desktop/src/app-source.mjs:183–203` uses the existing framed archive extraction, which records no extended attributes (`app-archive.mjs:23–40`). Activation copies that extracted app and renames it over the installed app (`app-lifecycle.mjs:250–273`) without transferring the installed app's quarantine attribute. The old attribute survives only on the retained previous app. Thus a successful unsigned whole-app update silently replaces a quarantined installation with an unquarantined one, violating this PR's maintained OS-permission contract.

**Concrete isolated repro:** `node quarantine-repro.mjs` in this report directory. It marks a temporary fixture app with `com.apple.quarantine`, uses the actual `packApp`/`unpackApp`, supplies a valid candidate-bound unsigned integrity proof, and calls the actual `DesktopAppLifecycle.activate()` with only worker ownership simulated as absent. `quarantine-result.json` records before/previous xattr read status **0**, staged/installed-after status **1** (attribute absent), and `fingerprintMatches: true`. No executable launch or Gatekeeper acceptance is claimed.

Preserve the applicable quarantine state through staging/replacement and recovery, and cover this OS-metadata boundary with a focused fixture. This requires no publisher certificates, paid account, notarization, or new physical-authenticator gate.

No additional documented-standard violations or material non-tooling Fowler smells found. Recovery retains exact checked-manifest binding; publication retains immutable asset snapshots and verified upload streams. Native stores and historical evidence remain outside this change.

## Spec

No separate spec findings. Signing/key-pin/Apple assessment prerequisites were removed from maintained release consumers, publisher, workflows, package recipes and instructions. Candidate/version/source/tooling checks, archive SHA256/size verification, complete inventory, stable asset-bound approval, nightly activation/ordering, source semantic intake, ownership, policy and rollback remain. Desktop uses its custom complete-app updater; Squirrel assumptions were not applied.

The quarantine mismatch is reported under Standards against the explicit maintained contract, not duplicated here. Pending actual native ad-hoc packaging and quarantined first-launch validation are honestly scoped in the implementation report; they are not a blanket implementation acceptance gate. No paid infrastructure, live provider, or physical-passkey requirement is added by this review.

